  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 170,
    "sourceUrl": "https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf",
    "note": "IEEE 802.3at PoE+ on twenty-four of the forty-eight copper ports at up to 30 W per port against a 170 W budget - the same 170 W as the GS1900-24HPv2, spread over twice the copper, so a 48-port chassis here powers no more PDs than the 24-port one. The datasheet states counts only (24 x GbE PoE RJ-45 ports, 24 x GbE RJ-45 ports) without naming port numbers, so ports 1-24 are modelled as the PSE group in the model list left-to-right order; that numbering is the one inferred field, while the counts and the budget are cited."
  },
  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 100000,
    "kind": "switching capacity",
    "note": "Zyxel quotes 100 Gbps switching capacity and 74 Mpps forwarding rate, with a 525 K packet buffer, an 8 K MAC address table and 9 K jumbo frames."
  },
  "sourceUrl": "https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf",
  "notes": "Zyxel GS1900 Series datasheet (dated 16/11/22) https://static.us.zyxel.com/pdf/2024/switch/ds_GS1900-10HP.pdf; specification table https://www.zyxel.com/global/en/products/switch/gs1900-series/specification. Management and switching features from the datasheet feature list and the GS1900 Series User Guide V2.90 Edition 2 https://download.zyxel.com/GS1900-48HPv2/user_guide/GS1900-48HPv2_V2.90_Ed2.pdf. There is NO console port and no CLI anywhere in the series: management is the web GUI, SNMP v1/v2/v3, RMON 1/2/3/9, syslog, LLDP/LLDP-MED, 802.1x, RADIUS and TACACS+, which is why no device here declares cli. Forty-eight-port PoE model: total port count 50 = 48 RJ45 (24 PoE) + 2 SFP, 170 W budget, 220.5 W maximum consumption, 441 x 270 x 44 mm, 3.55 kg, smart fan (27.8 dBA idle / 44.7 dBA maximum). The datasheet ordering table lists GS190048HPV2-EU0101F / -US0101F at hardware revision B1."
}
